Error: The following argument was not expected: -u
Run models on this machine or on your RunAnywhere account

Usage: wally [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Chat:
  run                         Run a model
  serve                       Serve a model over an OpenAI-compatible API

Models:
  models list                 List downloaded models (--all for the catalog)
  models show                 Show a model's details
  models pull                 Download a model
  models rm                   Delete a downloaded model
  models default              Show or set the default model for coding tools

Coding tools:
  claude-code                 Open Claude Code with a model
  claude-desktop              Open Claude Desktop with a model
  opencode                    Open opencode with a model
  hermes                      Open Hermes with a model
  openclaw                    Open OpenClaw with a model
  deepseek                    Open DeepSeek Harness with a model

Account:
  account login               Sign in through the browser
  account logout              Sign out and revoke the session
  account whoami              Show the signed-in account
  account usage               Show remaining credit and the last day's spend

Wally:
  about                       Versions, backends, paths and account
  update                      Update wally to the latest release
  uninstall                   Remove wally, its models and its config

Options:
  -h, --help                  Show help
  -V, --version               Show the wally version
      --json                  Print results as JSON
  -v, --verbose               Debug logging on stderr
  -q, --quiet                 Errors only
      --no-progress           Disable progress rendering
      --no-color              Disable colored --help output
      --home TEXT             Where models live (default $RUNANYWHERE_HOME or
                              ~/.local/share/runanywhere)

Get started:
  wally models pull qwen3-0.6b && wally run qwen3-0.6b
  wally account login && wally opencode --cloud -m glm-5.3-flash

Run "wally <command> --help" for details.
